    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\nI implemented the rule with a single, minimal change to `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`: added one disjunct to the existing conflict guard that counts owners already in the new owner's city and returns `409 CONFLICT` when that count is \u2265 50.\n\n```java\n|| owners.stream().filter(existing -> existing.getCity().equalsIgnoreCase(owner.getCity())).count() >= 50\n```\n\nStructural-impact rationale:\n- **One file, one function** \u2014 no new methods or classes, so the file-count multiplier stays at 1 and only one function's WMC_other is paid.\n- **Minimal changed lines / CC** \u2014 reused the already-fetched `owners` collection and folded the check into the existing `if` that already returns `CONFLICT`, adding just a single condition rather than a new branch-and-return block.",
